/* book Worked example: Q: A single-start square-thread screw has dm = 24 mm and lead 6 mm. It raises W = 20 kN with μ = 0.15. Find α, the raising and lowering torques and the efficiency, and say whether it self-locks. Then add a collar with μc = 0.12 and Rm = 20 mm.
   1. tan α = 6/(π × 24) = 0.0796, so α = 4.55°; tan φ = 0.15, so φ = 8.53°.
   2. Tr = (20 000 × 12)(0.15 + 0.0796)/(1 − 0.15 × 0.0796) = 240 000 × 0.2324 = 55 800 N·mm = 55.8 N·m.
   3. Tl = 240 000 × (0.15 − 0.0796)/(1 + 0.15 × 0.0796) = 16 700 N·mm. Positive, so φ > α and the screw self-locks.
   4. η = 20 000 × 6/(2π × 55 800) = 0.342.
   5. Collar: Tc = 0.12 × 20 000 × 20 = 48 000 N·mm. Total raising torque 103.8 N·m; η = 20 000 × 6/(2π × 103 800) = 0.184.
   Answer: α = 4.55°, Tr = 55.8 N·m, Tl = 16.7 N·m, η = 34.2 %, self-locking; with the collar, 103.8 N·m and 18.4 %. */
