/* book Worked example: Q: A spring of D = 50 mm, d = 6 mm and 10 active coils carries 500 N. G = 80 000 MPa. Find the Wahl factor, largest shear stress, deflection and rate.
   1. C = 50/6 = 8.33.
   2. K = (33.33 − 1)/(33.33 − 4) + 0.615/8.33 = 1.102 + 0.074 = 1.176.
   3. τ = 1.176 × 8 × 500 × 50/(π × 6³) = 1.176 × 294.7 = 346.6 MPa.
   4. δ = 8 × 500 × 50³ × 10/(80 000 × 6⁴) = 5.0 × 10⁹/1.037 × 10⁸ = 48.2 mm.
   5. k = 500/48.2 = 10.4 N/mm.
   Answer: K = 1.176, τ = 347 MPa, δ = 48.2 mm, k = 10.4 N/mm. */
