/* book Worked example 2: Q: Design a helical compression spring (squared and ground ends) for a maximum load of 1000 N with a deflection of 25 mm at that load. Take C = 6, permissible shear 420 MPa, G = 81 370 MPa. Find d, D, Na, Ls, Lf and pitch, and check surge for a 10 Hz cam.
   1. K = 23/20 + 0.615/6 = 1.2525.
   2. From τ = K·8WC/(πd²): d² = 1.2525 × 8 × 1000 × 6/(π × 420) = 45.56, d = 6.75 mm. Take d = 7 mm, so D = 42 mm (τ = 390.5 MPa).
   3. Na = Gd⁴δ/(8WD³) = 81 370 × 2401 × 25/(8 × 1000 × 74 088) = 8.24. Take 8 active coils: δ = 24.3 mm, k = 41.2 N/mm.
   4. Nt = 8 + 2 = 10, Ls = 10 × 7 = 70 mm.
   5. Lf = 70 + 24.3 + 0.15 × 24.3 = 97.9 mm; take 98 mm. Pitch = 98/9 = 10.9 mm.
   6. Lf/D = 98/42 = 2.3 < 4, so no buckling guide is needed.
   7. fn = (0.007/(2π × 0.042² × 8))√(81.37 × 10⁹/(2 × 7850)) = 180 Hz, 18 times the 10 Hz cam.
   Answer: d = 7 mm, D = 42 mm, 8 active and 10 total coils, Ls = 70 mm, Lf = 98 mm, pitch 10.9 mm, fn = 180 Hz. */
