/* book exam traps: Leaving out the Wahl factor. At C = 6 it adds 25 % to the stress. | Using the outside diameter as D. D is the mean coil diameter, from wire centre to wire centre. | Using total coils in the deflection formula. Only active coils deflect. | Mixing units in the surge formula: it needs metres, pascals and kg/m³, while the stress formula is in N and mm. | Rounding Na up without rechecking δ. More coils make the spring softer, so the deflection changes. */
